# Harness Contract

The commitments every harness workflow shares. Each carrier skill or agent
cites this file and keeps only its **role-specific consequence** — the
consequence lives at the site, the rule lives here.

## Conflict rule

- **Tactics** (`writing-*` skills, `agent_harness_rails/rules/*.mdc`) win on **specific HOW**.
- **Compass** (`agent_harness_rails/skills/rails-omakase-compass/SKILL.md`) wins
  on **whether** the solution shape matches omakase intent — unless the user or
  plan has **explicitly** documented a different shape (API-first, SPA); then
  that documented exception governs.

## Harness rules beat application patterns

Apply harness rules to the work at hand — do not inherit anti-patterns from the
surrounding codebase. If every controller in the app calls service objects but
this task adds a new action, write the action using model logic per
`agent_harness_rails/rules/services.mdc`, not by calling into an existing
service object. An established application pattern is not a justification — it
may be exactly the debt worth naming. Each carrier defines what its role does
when the surrounding pattern genuinely blocks the correct approach.

## Subagent context isolation

A subagent sees only its prompt and the files it reads — never the parent
chat. Facts the parent holds but the prompt omits do not exist for the
subagent.

## Supplementary references

Two fetch-based skills supplement the harness when the compass, the scoped
**`writing-*`** skills, and **`agent_harness_rails/rules/*.mdc`** leave a
**Rails best-practice** gap:

- **`agent_harness_rails/skills/referencing-unofficial-37signals-guide/SKILL.md`** — supplemental patterns and philosophy from the third-party community guide.
- **`agent_harness_rails/skills/referencing-rails-guides/SKILL.md`** — authoritative Rails API and feature docs (GitHub API index first, then the specific guide).

Both **inform** harness conventions — they never override them; tactics in this
harness win on HOW, per the conflict rule above. Each carrier declares whether
the consult is **optional** or **required** for its workflow. If a fetch fails,
**report the failure** per that skill — never invent or assert content as if it
came from the source.
